<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<city>
  <ticket uid="0" name="20min" price="1" probability="35" upsell="25" />
  <ticket uid="1" name="60min" price="2" probability="55" upsell="8" />
  <ticket uid="2" name="24h" price="12" probability="5" upsell="2" />
  <ticket uid="3" name="7d" price="60" probability="1" upsell="0" />
  <!-- 

1) City tag is active
2) You roll to a stop with 20 people in your bus, 6 of them leaving and 50 new people boarding
3) You have a list of tickets with unique uids and various stats
4) Ticket uid 0 has a probability 35% of boarding passengers, meaning that 35% of 50 buy this ticket
5) It also has a 25% chance of an upsell to the next ticket (=uid 1)
6) 25% of 35% of 50 is 4,375 people. You cannot have 0,375 person buy a ticket, so you trim all decimals (=4)
7) Therefore 4 people might get and upsell. Flip a coin for each person. If true, then they buy the ticket with the next uid (=uid 1), if not, they buy the current ticket (uid = 0)
8) Repeat steps 4-7 for all tickets
9) 14 people you already have in your vehicle don't buy new tickets, they exist just as they are

We don't care that passengers that got an upsell leave at the next stop - it's a "city" they might take another line we don't see

Not all passengers buy tickets and that is fine. 
			-->
</city>